From 2de3094d683b5e0aca44a2ea0796c39532a4a2a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bj=C3=B6rn=20Strausmann?= <projects@strausmann.ch>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:22:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: request a source keyframe when a WebRTC viewer sends
 PLI/FIR

Some sources (UniFi Protect) ignore RTCP PLI/FIR and emit an IDR frame
only once per GOP, so a WebRTC viewer that joins or loses a frame waits
up to several seconds for a picture. They do emit an IDR frame when a new
RTSP session sets up the video track.

- webrtc: read PLI/FIR from the RTCP feedback of each sender and forward
  a keyframe request for video tracks to the stream's producer.
- rtsp: new source option #keyframe=resetup. RequestKeyframe opens a short
  helper session (OPTIONS, DESCRIBE, SETUP, TEARDOWN, always
  TCP-interleaved, no redirect): at most one per second and never two at
  the same time per source connection, overall deadline, aborted by Stop.
  Errors carry only stage and error class, never URL, credentials or
  host:port. WebSocket transports are refused.
- tcp: bound the TLS handshake by the dial timeout, add DialContext, and
  reject invalid or oversized (> 16 MiB) Content-Length values instead of
  panicking.
- webrtc: keep the RTCP read loop alive across a single unparsable packet
  (ends on read end or after 64 consecutive errors).

Off by default; sources without the option behave as before.
